---
/*
 * Avatar 2, The Open Calendar. Tim's brief, 2026-09-24.
 * Ads A2-1 (own schedule) and A2-2 (guest room) point here.
 *
 * Words to use: your own bed, drives like a pickup, easy, comfortable, real
 * bathroom, heat and air, see the country, visit the grandkids, on your
 * schedule. Never: off-grid, boondocking, rugged, overlanding, golden years,
 * seniors, or anything that tells them they are old.
 *
 * Held back until Tim confirms: "a real person answers after delivery",
 * "a bed that stays made" and the delivery walkthrough. The brief also points
 * this buyer at Signature Pre-Builds; staging dropped Signature for Tailored
 * and Bespoke on 2026-09-25, so this page follows staging.
 */
import AdLanding from "../components/AdLanding.astro";
---

<AdLanding
	slug="retire"
	title="See The Country On Your Own Schedule | Papago Vans"
	description="Custom Sprinter camper vans with a real bed, a bathroom, heat and air. Built to order in Mesa, AZ. Van included in every price."
	hero={{
		img: "/lp/collage-feature-2.webp",
		alt: "A couple sitting at the swivel-seat table of a Papago van, coffee in hand, side door open",
		eyebrow: "Custom Sprinter campers · Mesa, AZ",
		h1: "See The Country On Your Own Schedule",
		sub: "A custom Sprinter camper with your own bed, a real bathroom, heat and air. Built to order in Mesa, Arizona.",
		checks: [
			"About the length of a crew-cab pickup, and drives like one",
			"Heat and air that run without plugging in",
			"RVIA certified, veteran owned, 4.7 stars from 70+ reviews",
		],
	}}
	pairs={[
		{
			problem: "Motorhomes are too big to enjoy driving.",
			solution: "A Sprinter is about the length of a crew-cab pickup.",
			body: "No towing, no 40-foot motorhome, nothing to unhitch. It parks in a normal space and drives like your truck, with a real bed and bathroom inside.",
		},
		{
			problem: "Plenty of campers only run the air when they are plugged in.",
			solution: "Heat and air that work wherever you parked.",
			body: "A lithium battery bank and solar on the roof run the heat and the air, and it charges while you drive. A cold morning in Utah and an August afternoon in Texas are both fine.",
		},
		{
			problem: "The biggest fear with any builder: the deposit, and then silence.",
			solution: "Come walk our shop in Mesa.",
			body: "RVIA certified, veteran owned, and 4.7 stars from more than 70 verified reviews. Every build carries our 1-year craftsmanship warranty. In Arizona? See vans being built before you decide anything.",
		},
	]}
	scene={{
		img: "/lp/scene-open-calendar.webp",
		alt: "A woman cooking at the galley counter of a Sprinter, induction burner going, slider door open on the trees",
		eyebrow: "A Month In Yours",
		h2: "Visit The Grandkids. Bring Your Own Guest Room.",
		paras: [
			"Your bed, your bathroom and your coffee, parked in their driveway. No hotel, no air mattress, and you leave when you are ready, not when checkout says so.",
			"Stay a night at a national park or stay a week. Drawers that stay shut on the highway hold a week of clothes, so you unpack once. Dinner gets cooked on your own counter instead of found off an exit ramp.",
		],
	}}
	reviews={[
		{ name: "Mike and Melanie", quote: "There is absolutely no way that we could have found a better company to build out our custom dream van to see the USA. Hands down, they're the best in the business. We give our highest recommendation (10+ stars)." },
		{ name: "Wendy F.", quote: "We have been 100% happy right from our beginning inquiry phone call to waving goodbye as we drove our newly finished custom van out the driveway." },
		{ name: "Debi L.", quote: "I was very anxious since I was not in the same state, but they went above and beyond my wildest dreams and created an absolutely stunning van for me." },
	]}
	included={{
		h2: "What Makes It Easy To Live In",
		items: [
			["Your own bed", "Every night, in the same van, with your own pillows"],
			["A real bathroom", "Indoor shower and toilet in most floor plans"],
			["Heat and air", "Run from the battery, no campground plug needed"],
			["Hot and cold running water", "A real sink and a hot shower"],
			["A kitchen you will cook in", "Butcher block counter, induction cooktop option"],
			["Storage that stays shut", "Drawers and cabinets built for the highway"],
			["Easy to drive", "About the length of a crew-cab pickup"],
			["The Sprinter itself", "Sourced through our dealers, included in the price"],
			["RVIA certified", "The standard lenders, insurers and campgrounds look for"],
			["1-year craftsmanship warranty", "On everything we build"],
			["Service Department in Mesa", "Repairs and upgrades from the shop that built it"],
			["Veteran owned", "Built by people who show up"],
		],
	}}
	faqs={[
		{ q: "Is it hard to drive?", a: "No. A Sprinter is about the length of a crew-cab pickup and drives like one. There is nothing to tow and nothing to unhitch, and it fits a normal parking space." },
		{ q: "Can I have a bathroom and a shower inside?", a: "Yes. An enclosed indoor shower and toilet fit in most of our floor plans, and every build can carry an exterior shower as well." },
		{ q: "What happens if something needs fixing after delivery?", a: "Every build carries our 1-year craftsmanship warranty, and our Service Department in Mesa handles repairs and upgrades." },
		{ q: "Can we come see the shop?", a: "Please do. Call us and we will set a time to walk you through vans being built." },
		{ q: "How much does it cost?", a: "A Tailored build runs $180,000 to $250,000, Mercedes-Benz Sprinter included. Most of the range is chassis length and the equipment you choose." },
		{ q: "Can we finance it?", a: "Yes, through our partner Hearth. We can finance the van and the build together, or the build on its own." },
	]}
	close={{
		h2: "You Earned The Time. Now Take The Trip.",
		p: "Tell us where you want to go first. We will put a real number on your van, Sprinter included.",
	}}
/>
